  {Extra  loops.  {II}.  {O}n  loops  with  identities of\n      176                       {B}ol\\texttt{\\symbol{45}}{M}oufang type},\n      177   journal =          {Publ. Math. Debrecen},\n      178   volume =           {16},\n      179   year =             {1969},\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMoufang loops that share associator and three quarters of their multiplication tables - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/math/0701710v1)\nciteturn16search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; ## Moufang loops that share associator and three quarters of their multiplication tables ... Journal: Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36 (2006), no. 2, 425-455 ... We present these constructions in a compact way, and generalize them to Moufang loops, using loop extensions.\n# arXiv++ Combinatorics\n\nBrowse math.CO papers from arXiv\n\n## Moufang loops that share associator and three quarters of their multiplication tables\n\nAleš Drápal, Petr Vojtěchovský\n\nPublished: 2007-01-24\n\nComments: 20 pages\n\nNote:\n\nJournal: Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36 (2006), no. 2, 425-455\n\nPublication:\n\ngroup\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nTwo constructions due to Drápal produce a group by modifying exactly one quarter of the Cayley table of another group. We present these constructions in a compact way, and generalize them to Moufang loops, using loop extensions. Both constructions preserve associators, the associator subloop, and the nucleus. We conjecture that two Moufang 2-loops of finite order $n$ with equivalent associator can be connected by a series of constructions similar to ours, and offer empirical evidence that this is so for $n=16$, 24, 32; the only interesting cases with $n\\le 32$. We further investigate the way the constructions affect code loops and loops of type $M(G, 2)$. The paper closes with several conjectures and research questions concerning the distance of Moufang loops, classification of small Moufang loops, and generalizations of the two constructions.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPetr Vojtechovsky (Papers in research journals) (https://cs.du.edu/~petr/in_research_journals.html)\nciteturn16search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Moufang loops that share associator and three quarters of their multiplication tables ... Drapal, Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36 (2006), no. 2, 425-455\n  52. The Moufang loops of order 64 and 81\nwith G. P. Nagy, J. Symbolic Computation 42 (2007), no. 9, 871-883\n     > The GAP code used in the paper to obtain Moufang loops of order 64 and 81\n     > Search output for Moufang loops of order 64, extensions of at least 3-generated Moufang loops of order 32, except E_32\n     > Search output for code loops of order 64\n  53. Powers and alternative laws\nwith N. Ormes, Comment. Math. Univ. Carolin. 48 (2007), no. 1, 25-40\n  54. Colored graphs without colorful cycles\nwith R. N. Ball and A. Pultr, Combinatorica 27 (2007), no. 4, 407-427\n  55. C-loops: Extensions and constructions\nwith M. K. Kinyon and J. D. Phillips, Journal of Algebra and its Applications 6 (2007), no. 1, 1-20\n  56. Right division in groups, Dedekind-Frobenius group matrices, and Ward quasigroups\nwith K. W. Johnson, Abh. Math. Sem. Univ. Hamburg 75 (2006), 121-136\n  57. Toward the classification of Moufang loops of order 64\nEuropean J. Combin. 27, issue 3 (April 2006), 444-460\n     > The GAP library used to obtain the Moufang loops in the paper\n  58. C-loops: An introduction\nwith J. D. Phillips, Publicationes Mathematicae Debrecen 68 (2006), nos. 1-2, 115-137\n  59. Moufang loops that share associator and three quarters of their multiplication tables\nwith A. Drapal, Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36 (2006), no. 2, 425-455\n     > Term formulas for the cyclic and dihedral constructions (alternative proof mentioned in the paper)\n  60. The varieties of quasigroups of Bol-Moufang type: An equational reasoning approach\nwith J. D. Phillips, J. Algebra 293 (2005), 17-33\n     > OTTER generated proofs\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Moufang Loops that Share Associator and Three Quarters of Their Multiplication Tables (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2135105_Moufang_Loops_That_Share_Associator_And_Three_Quarters_Of_Their_Multiplication_Tables)\nciteturn16search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.6 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Moufang Loops that Share Associator and Three Quarters of Their Multiplication Tables ...   * Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36(2):425-455 ... Suppose that L is a Moufang loop whose associator is equivalent to the\n\n# Moufang Loops that Share Associator and Three Quarters of Their Multiplication Tables\n\n  * April 2006\n  * Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics 36(2):425-455\n\nDOI:10.1216/rmjm/1181069461\n\nAuthors:\n\nAles Drapal\n\n  * Charles University\n\nPetr Vojtěchovský\n\n  * University of Denver\n\nImage\n\nDownload full-text PDFRead full-text\n\n## Abstract\n\nTwo constructions due to Dr\\'apal produce a group by modifying exactly one quarter of the Cayley table of another group. We present these constructions in a compact way, and generalize them to Moufang loops, using loop extensions. Both constructions preserve associators, the associator subloop, and the nucleus. We conjecture that two Moufang 2-loops of finite order n with equivalent associator can be connected by a series of constructions similar to ours, and offer empirical evidence that this is so for n=16, 24, 32; the only interesting cases with $n\\le 32$. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGAP: pkg/loops/doc/loops_bib.xml | Fossies (https://fossies.org/linux/gap/pkg/loops/doc/loops_bib.xml)\nciteturn16search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;       